<title>USA: IMF official warns against EMU delay.</title>
<headline>IMF official warns against EMU delay.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massimo Russo, special adviser to IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus, said Saturday that a delay in Stage Three of European monetary union would endanger progress in forming a single European currency.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference, Russo said: &quot;We at the IMF believe a delay in Stage Three would lead to substantial dangers.&quot;</p>
<p>Russo said a delay in EMU could lead to the project being shelved for some time, making it hard for countries to continue their efforts towards qualifying for EMU entry.</p>
<p>He added that a delay could also lead to turmoil in financial markets.</p>
<p>EMU is scheduled to begin January 1, 1999.</p>
</text>
